Patch 69 -- p71: the whole context_apply_draw_state() native, on an MS-layout island.

Rejected by measurement, kept because the rejection is the result. Entry 39's
boundary was retried on an island built by clang -mms-bitfields, so the nine hard
ABI failures that invalidated p69 are gone. It still rendered black: the bounded
shader witness read current program 0, program pipeline 0 and
GL_INVALID_OPERATION in 171 of 171 samples. The island links a second copy of
glsl_shader.c, whose nine separable-program entry pointers are its own, so the
native shader phase bound nothing. Phase D references all nine; B and C none.

Section 13.3 of docs/briefs/MGS2_PHASE_A_NATIVE_MEASURED_2026-08-21.md has the
run. Do not re-apply without solving the duplicated separable pointers first.

